// PARKED — see ../README.md, "What is parked, and why".
//
// Zoo edge: IMM -> POWER (compilation). Two separate obstacles, both found by
// running the query rather than by reading it:
//
// 1. SHAPE. As originally parked the assert was `imm::psc <= power-weak::ar`,
//    against a single ar step. Power's axiom is acyclic(ar), so what has to
//    hold is that every psc edge is an ar *path* — the sibling TSO and ARMv8
//    queries have the closure (tso*, ob*) and this one did not. That alone
//    explains the parked counterexample; it was never a hole in the mapping.
//
// 2. VACUITY, which is why fixing the shape does not settle the edge. With the
//    closure the query passes in under a second — but so does everything else,
//    because kat/power-weak.kat's ar carries the term `eco*;po?;eco*`, and eco*
//    contains the identity, so ar contains po outright. Confirmed directly:
//
//        assert po <= power-weak::ar+        // HOLDS
//        assert sc::sc <= power-weak::ar+    // HOLDS
//
//    acyclic(ar) is therefore at least as strong as SC for this rendering, and
//    any relation built over po/rf/mo/fr is contained in ar+ for free. The same
//    term, and the same degeneracy, is in kat/power-fm-simpl.kat and
//    kat/power-fm-simpl-full.kat. (The TSO and ARMv8 targets are clean: `po <=
//    tso::tso+` and `po <= arm8::ob+` are both refuted.)
//
// The two renderings without that term — kat/power-fm.kat and
// kat/power-fm-orig.kat — are non-degenerate, and against them the query is
// refuted on a fence-vocabulary gap: IMM's psc relates two SC fences directly
// (FSC ; po ; FSC), while Power's sync is stated between accesses
// ([R|W]; po; [F;SC]; po; [R|W]), so a bare fence-to-fence po pair has no
// counterpart. Counterexample against power-fm:
//
//     [SC&F] ===> po [SC&F]
//
// Settling the edge means restating Power's fence ordering so fence endpoints
// are covered — the manual rewriting the paper reports for its own Power
// queries (§3.7) — not adding a closure. Leaving the query in the shape that is
// at least diagnostic: non-degenerate target, no vacuity.
include "../../kat/imm.kat"
include "../../kat/power-fm.kat"

assert imm::psc <= power-fm::ar+
